From: Alexander Hansen <alexander.hansen@9elements.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 15:24:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] allow for updating spi partitions

Some SPI flashes are partitioned to allow for A/B firmware updates
without requiring multiple chips.

Devicetree example:
```
flash@1 {
compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
reg = <1>;
partitions {
 compatible = "fixed-partitions";
 #address-cells = <1>;
 #size-cells = <1>;

 host-prime@0 {
  label = "host-prime";
  reg = <0x0 0x2000000>;
 };
 host-second@2000000 {
  label = "host-second";
  reg = <0x2000000 0x2000000>;
 };
};
};
```

This shows up in sysfs like below:

```
/dev/mtd13  name=host-prime   offset=0         size=33554432
/dev/mtd14  name=host-second  offset=33554432  size=33554432
SPI sysfs directory: /sys/class/spi_master/spi1/spi1.1/mtd/
```

Adjust the code to allow for configuring the partition to be updated.
In case no partition is configured (empty string property value), the
update should work as before.

Tested: confirmed that the correct flash partition was chosen during the
update process

```
/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/chassis/chassis/UEFIPrimary:
  xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.HostSPIFlash
    Name               s  "UEFIPrimary"
    Offset             t  33554432
    SPIControllerIndex t  1
    SPIDeviceIndex     t  1
    Type               s  "HostSPIFlash"
```

```
 curl -k -sS --connect-timeout 15 --max-time 180 \
    -u "$RF_USER:$RF_PASSWORD" -D - \
    -F 'UpdateParameters={"Targets":["/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory/UEFIPrimary_7453"],"@Redfish.OperationApplyTime":"Immediate"};type=application/json' \
    -F 'UpdateFile=@pldm-package-hpe-proliant-g11-d360-host-empty.bin;type=application/octet-stream' \
    "$BMC/redfish/v1/UpdateService/update-multipart"
```

