At 15:43:55, flashcp was still running on /dev/mtd14 and D-Bus
still showed UEFIPrimary_4469 Activation=Activating and Progress=30.
This was a Redfish task timeout, not a request to terminate flashcp.
The update was allowed to finish.

So in regards to the redfish task timeout there may be extra work needed
but it's unrelated to this patch which only deals with partition
selection. The update ran around 9 minutes but the timeout allowed for
only 5 minutes. Overall the update was successful on part of the
updater.

